# BWB Climbing App Commit Template
#
# Format: <type>[scope]: <description>
#
# Types:
#   feat:     A new feature
#   fix:      A bug fix
#   docs:     Documentation only changes
#   style:    Changes that don't affect code meaning
#   refactor: Code change that neither fixes a bug nor adds a feature
#   test:     Adding missing tests or correcting existing tests
#   chore:    Changes to build process or auxiliary tools
#
# Scopes (for BWB):
#   ui:       Frontend components, styling, user interface
#   api:      Backend routes, server logic, API endpoints
#   db:       Database schema, migrations, Prisma
#   auth:     Authentication, authorization, middleware
#   docs:     Documentation files
#   test:     Test files and testing utilities
#   deploy:   Deployment, build scripts, CI/CD
#   deps:     Dependency updates
#   hof:      Hall of Fame domain logic
#   data:     Data import, export, seeding
#   admin:    Admin area features
#   infra:    Infrastructure, Docker, hosting
#   tooling:  Developer tooling and scripts
#   legal:    LICENSE, NOTICE, LICENSES/, licensing text
#
# The authoritative list is scope-enum in commitlint.config.cjs.
#
# Examples:
#   feat(ui): add user profile component
#   fix(api): resolve authentication timeout
#   docs(deploy): update deployment guide
#   style(ui): improve navigation spacing
#
# Remember:
# - Use present tense ("add" not "added")
# - Use imperative mood ("move cursor" not "moves cursor")
# - First line should be 50 characters or less
# - Reference issues and pull requests liberally after the first line
# - Consider the impact on automatic versioning:
#   feat: → MINOR bump, fix: → PATCH bump, BREAKING CHANGE: → MAJOR bump
